{"metadata":{"title":"Displaying Products","role":"collectionGroup","modules":[{"name":"FlareUI"}]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FlareUI"},{"text":" provides an easy way to display different kinds of products with a single line of code. To display a set of products to the user, just pass a collection of identifiers to the ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/flare.FlareUI\/documentation\/FlareUI\/ProductsView","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["ProductsView(ids: [\"com.company.product_id_1\", \"com.company.product_id_2\"])"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Once ","type":"text"},{"code":"ProductsView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" fetches these products from the App Store, it will display them to the user. If the products can’t be fetched for any reason, the ","type":"text"},{"code":"ProductsView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" shows a message to the user that the App Store is not available.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"By default, all Flare views use cached data if available; otherwise, they fetch the data. If you want to change this behavior, please read more about Flare configuration "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"link","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"type":"aside","style":"important","name":"Important"},{"text":"UIKit","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"UIKit"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FlareUI"},{"type":"text","text":" package provides wrappers for the UIKit views. It can be easily integrated into UIKit environments using "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/flare.FlareUI\/documentation\/FlareUI\/ProductsViewController","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let productsVC = ProductsViewController(ids: [\"com.company.product_id_1\", \"com.company.product_id_2\"])","let nav = UINavigationController(rootViewController: productsVC)","present(nav, animated: true)"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ProductsViewController"},{"type":"text","text":" is backed by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ProductsView"},{"type":"text","text":", and its behavior is the same."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Customization","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Customization"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The appearance of the displayed products can be customized using "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiftUI\/View\/productViewStyle(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":". There are predefined styles for different platforms: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LargeProductStyle"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/flare.FlareUI\/documentation\/FlareUI\/CompactProductStyle","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can also create your own style. For this, please, read "},{"overridingTitle":"How to Create a Custom Product Style","type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/flare.FlareUI\/documentation\/FlareUI\/creating-custom-product-style","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"text":"How to Create a Custom Product Style","type":"text"}],"isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Custom Buttons","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Custom-Buttons"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you have restorable products, the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ProductsView"},{"type":"text","text":" can show a restore button to the customer. For this, you can use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiftUI\/View\/storeButton(_:types:)-4x8yd"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/flare.FlareUI\/documentation\/FlareUI\/ProductsViewController\/storeButton(_:types:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ SwiftUI","","ProductsView(ids: [\"com.company.product_id_1\", \"com.company.product_id_2\"])","    .storeButton(.visible, types: .restore)"]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ UIKit","","let productsVC = ProductsViewController(ids: [\"com.company.product_id_1\", \"com.company.product_id_2\"])","productsVC.storeButton(.visible, types: [.restore])"]}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/flare.FlareUI\/documentation\/FlareUI"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Articles","title":"Articles","identifiers":["doc:\/\/flare.FlareUI\/documentation\/FlareUI\/creating-custom-product-style","doc:\/\/flare.FlareUI\/documentation\/FlareUI\/handling-transactions"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Learn how to display a set of products to a user."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/flareui\/displaying-products"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/flare.FlareUI\/documentation\/FlareUI\/displaying-products"},"kind":"article","references":{"link":{"identifier":"link","title":"here","type":"link","titleInlineContent":[{"text":"here","type":"text"}],"url":"link"},"doc://flare.FlareUI/documentation/FlareUI/ProductsViewController":{"url":"\/documentation\/flareui\/productsviewcontroller","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ProductsViewController","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A view for displaying multiple products.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/flare.FlareUI\/documentation\/FlareUI\/ProductsViewController","type":"topic","title":"ProductsViewController","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ProductsViewController","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://f